## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The searcher is most commonly a renter in the **middle of a fixed-term lease** (typically 12 months) who has received a job relocation offer, experienced a significant life change (breakup, new roommate situation, financial hardship, medical need), or is living in an apartment that has become unacceptable due to maintenance failures. They are in the **decision stage**: they have already identified that they may need to leave, and they want to understand what it will cost them before committing to that decision. They expect a structured, plain-language explanation of consequences, legal options, and a realistic picture of their financial exposure, not a legal treatise. This audience skews toward renters in their late 20s through early 40s, often first-time or early-career renters who have not broken a lease before.

